# Review: Timeline

The spec was written from built code (D-2), and most of it holds. `Sheet.Chart` is its own object owned by
the sheet, with a tested migration from inline charts. The timeline is `Timeline` in `react-ui-plot`,
wrapped by plugin-sheet's `TimelineChart`. Its pure helpers (event parsing, scales, category grouping,
filter matching) have unit tests; the interactive parts (selection, ⌘-click solo, scale animation) do not.
The Presenter space replaces `{{timeline}}` with the chart's EID and is tested. The biggest gap is F-3: a
presented deck renders an `echo:` embed inside the slide layout, not over the whole viewport, and the deck's
key handler has no embed mode that limits it to Escape. Neither scenario has an automated test. The
`Chart` type also carries fields the spec omits (`today`, `fontSize`). Of 15 items: 6 done, 4 untested,
2 partial, 0 diverged, 3 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

